  Title: 'Mode Of Transmission:'
  Description: (Cloud and Fluid beam) Airborne transmission of aerosols and droplets
    is the major route of dissemination of the virus, which can enter the body through
    the respiratory tract by the nose and mouth. Transmission through direct and indirect
    contact also occurs and is most common via the hand-nose-hand route, followed
    by self-inoculation of nasal/conjunctival mucosa present on one's hands.
